    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0568" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2457</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)<anchor n="65" xml:id="d409-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-30">October 30,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Joe</hi>: I am much interested in the comments
                    contained in your letter of September 22, 1941<anchor n="65a" xml:id="d409-f2"/>
                    in regard to Prince Konoye. It seems a pity that during the time that he was
                    Premier there could not have been rallied in Japan a wider and stronger support
                    for a moderate and peaceful policy.</p>
                <p>I also have read with interest the copy, which you enclosed,<anchor n="66"
                        xml:id="d409-f3"/> of a letter addressed by you to a Japanese friend who had
                    asked for American sympathy and cooperation in the pursuit by Japan of “her
                    legitimate interests and aspirations”. It seems to me that in your letter you
                    covered admirably and comprehensively the subject of American attitude toward
                    relations with Japan. I appreciate your having sent me a copy of the letter.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin D. Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
